  "report": "Confirmed source defects:\n\n- **QA timeout aborts collection:** `round2.py:85` leaves `subprocess.TimeoutExpired` uncaught. The run loses its review/result receipt instead of recording missing QA as BLOCKED; retry then hits the recovery guard at line 144. Catch the timeout, preserve available evidence, and return a BLOCKED review receipt.\n\n- **Verdict precedence and hash binding are inconsistent:** `round2_checks.py:78–88` returns FAIL for validated STOP_SHIP even when `review_engine_matches=False`, but returns BLOCKED for a matching STOP_SHIP when a phase is incomplete. Both outcomes were reproduced with read-only, in-memory probes. Check hash binding before accepting a review verdict, and let a confirmed, matching STOP_SHIP take precedence over missing completion.\n\n- **Incomplete reviewer usage can appear complete:** `round2.py:115–118` checks only whether reviewer usage exists. A timed-out reviewer with counters from a prior completed turn produces `usage_complete=True`, reproduced in memory. Preserve those counters but mark totals partial unless reviewer execution completed and required counters are present.\n\nInspected the nine scoped Python modules, the three relevant regression files, round-2 protocol, actual report, brief, instructions, and recorded checks. All supplied snapshot hashes matched. The report correctly discloses B2/C1 failures, the 64.085-second interval, and unknown USD/human minutes.\n\nNo files changed or test suites rerun. Live timeout behavior, raw model traces, billing, and audit receipts were not independently observed; supplied checks also record a desktop failure due to missing `tkinter`.\n\nSLICE_REVIEW: STOP_SHIP",
